<title>USA: Optical Data downgraded.</title>
<headline>Optical Data downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volpe Welty &amp; Co analyst Paul Bloom said he cut his rating on Optical Data Systems Inc to buy from strong buy on concern about third quarter earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;After a conversation with Optical Data Systems, we are concerned that the company will not make our third quarter 1996 earnings per share estimate of $0.30,&quot; Bloom said in a research note.</p>
<p>The stock was down three at 20-1/4.  </p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
